  _push(`<div${ssrRenderAttrs(_attrs)}><h1 id="advanced-path-segments" tabindex="-1">Advanced path segments <a class="header-anchor" href="#advanced-path-segments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Advanced path segments&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The advanced geometry segment classes represent mathematically analyzable pieces of a path. They can sample points, calculate derivatives and unit tangents, reverse direction, transform themselves, and return accurate bounds.</p><div class="language-js vp-adaptive-theme line-numbers-mode"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">js</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#D73A49", "--shiki-dark": "#F97583" })}">import</span><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#24292E", "--shiki-dark": "#E1E4E8" })}"> {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#24292E", "--shiki-dark": "#E1E4E8" })}">  LineSegment, QuadraticSegment, CubicSegment, ArcSegment</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#24292E", "--shiki-dark": "#E1E4E8" })}">} </span><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#D73A49", "--shiki-dark": "#F97583" })}">from</span><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#032F62", "--shiki-dark": "#9ECBFF" })}"> &quot;math-diagrammer/geometry&quot;</span><span style="${ssrRenderStyle({ "--shiki-light": "#24292E", "--shiki-dark": "#E1E4E8" })}">;</span></span></code></pre><div class="line-numbers-wrapper" aria-hidden="true"><span class="line-number">1</span><br><span class="line-number">2</span><br><span class="line-number">3</span><br></div></div><p>The standard parameter <code>t</code> normally means:</p><ul><li><code>0</code>: segment start;</li><li><code>1</code>: segment end;</li><li>a value between them: a point along the segment.</li></ul><p>Line and Bézier methods do not clamp <code>t</code>, so values outside <code>[0, 1]</code> extrapolate. A degenerate <code>ArcSegment</code> is the exception: its <code>pointAt(t)</code> clamps before linearly interpolating.</p><h2 id="shared-segment-ideas" tabindex="-1">Shared segment ideas <a class="header-anchor" href="#shared-segment-ideas" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Shared segment ideas&quot;">​</a></h2><p>All four segment classes expose:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.pointAt(t)</code></td><td>Point at parameter <code>t</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.at(t)</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.pointAt(t)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.derivativeAt(t)</code></td><td>Non-normalized direction and speed</td></tr><tr><td><code>.tangentAt(t)</code></td><td>Normalized derivative; zero derivative becomes <code>(0, 0)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>.bounds()</code></td><td>Axis-aligned Bounds containing the segment</td></tr><tr><td><code>.reverse()</code></td><td>New segment traveling the opposite direction</td></tr><tr><td><code>.transform(matrix)</code></td><td>New transformed segment</td></tr><tr><td><code>.transformed(matrix)</code></td><td>Alias of <code>.transform(matrix)</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="linesegment" tabindex="-1">LineSegment <a class="header-anchor" href="#linesegment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;LineSegment&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="new-linesegment-start-end" tabindex="-1"><code>new LineSegment(start, end)</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#new-linesegment-start-end" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;\`new LineSegment(start, end)\`&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Converts both endpoints with <code>Point.from()</code> and freezes the result.</p><p>Properties:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.start</code></td><td>Starting Point</td></tr><tr><td><code>.end</code></td><td>Ending Point</td></tr></tbody></table>`);
