  _push(`<p>Returned object:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>center</code></td><td>Calculated Point</td></tr><tr><td><code>radiusX</code>, <code>radiusY</code></td><td>Absolute, possibly corrected radii</td></tr><tr><td><code>rotation</code></td><td>Rotation in radians</td></tr><tr><td><code>rotationDegrees</code></td><td>Original numeric degree value</td></tr><tr><td><code>startAngle</code></td><td>Ellipse-basis start angle</td></tr><tr><td><code>sweepAngle</code></td><td>Signed sweep angle</td></tr><tr><td><code>degenerate</code></td><td><code>true</code> for equal endpoints or a near-zero radius</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For a degenerate result, the center is the midpoint, both angles are zero, and the radii remain their absolute input values.</p><h2 id="bounds-helpers" tabindex="-1">Bounds helpers <a class="header-anchor" href="#bounds-helpers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Bounds helpers&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="segmentbounds-segment" tabindex="-1"><code>segmentBounds(segment)</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#segmentbounds-segment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;\`segmentBounds(segment)\`&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Calls <code>segment.bounds()</code>. It throws <code>TypeError(&quot;Expected a path segment with bounds().&quot;)</code> when the input is missing or has no callable <code>bounds</code> method.</p><h3 id="pathbounds-segments" tabindex="-1"><code>pathBounds(segments)</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#pathbounds-segments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;\`pathBounds(segments)\`&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Reduces a segment array into the union of every <code>segmentBounds()</code> result. An empty array returns <code>Bounds.empty()</code>.</p>`);
